            <ArticleTitle>[Not very commonplace throat pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>223-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Jugular vein suppurative thrombophlebitis or Lemierre's syndrome is a rare but distinct clinical entity. It should be considered in young, otherwise healthy adults with &quot;pharyngitis&quot; followed by high fever, painful swelling or pain in a latero-cervical area. Rapid and appropriate treatment is important to control this potentially fatal infection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
